+// Gears2-Native SDK patch 16 (job 117, notes/46 section 0c): the host path pairs an end ZPD with the active query only if
+// both use the same report address. XDK 7645's D3D (Gears of War 2) writes each query's BEGIN report at block+32 and
+// its END report at block+0, so every end "mismatches": the first one turns host queries off for the session and every
+// answer is the fake count. With this on (or with occlusion_query_no_fake), an end ZPD closes the active query whatever
+// its address. Off by default: on, it brings real culling and one blocking GPU round trip per query (200-280 a frame).
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(occlusion_query_end_any_address, false, "GPU/D3D12",
+                    "Occlusion queries: an end ZPD closes the active query even at a different report address");
